# Ignore rules for this repository.
#
# ⛔ .gitignore only applies to files git is not ALREADY tracking. Adding a line
# does not untrack what is already in. Check with: git ls-files

# -- secrets. Never committed, no exceptions ---------------------------------
# ⛔ Listed BEFORE the files exist, so one can never be staged by accident.
# A credential file added here after the fact was trackable in between.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
!.dev.vars.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*.token
.*_token
.*-token

# -- scratch and temporary work ---------------------------------------------
# .tmp/ holds the commit message file, the gate's pass record and any download.
.tmp/
tmp/
scratch/
.scratch/

# -- logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/

# -- local databases ---------------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# -- coverage and test output -----------------------------------------------
coverage/
.coverage
test-results/
.nyc_output/

# -- agent and assistant local files ----------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
CLAUDE.local.md

# -- Node, and anything that runs on it --------------------------------------
node_modules/
.npm/
dist/
build/
.cache/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache

# ⛔ A lockfile IS committed. It is what makes an install reproducible, and a
# project without one installs a different dependency tree every time.
# package-lock.json is listed here as a reminder, not as an ignore.

# Cloudflare Workers local state. Deleting this directory resets ALL local data.
.wrangler/
# The `cf` CLI's account cache and wrangler's sign-in are credential files.
.cloudflare/

# -- operating system and editor noise ---------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
.directory
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ⛔ WINDOWS RESERVED DEVICE NAMES. Two different things create one as a real
# file, and only the first is something you wrote:
#   1. your own redirect: 2>/dev/null under a shell that does not map it makes
#      a real file called nul, which git then tracks, which breaks git stash
#      outright, and which cannot be deleted by rm or by Python;
#   2. a tool's own argument list: some ssh wrappers pass
#      -o UserKnownHostsFile=NUL, and under Git Bash that is a filename.
# Ignoring the whole set is what stops the recurrence.
nul
CON
PRN
AUX
NUL
COM[1-9]
LPT[1-9]
CON.*
PRN.*
AUX.*
NUL.*
COM[1-9].*
LPT[1-9].*

# --- this project ---------------------------------------------------------
# The session resume file: written at every session start, never committed
# (docs/methodology/sessions.md).
RESUME.md
# Local secrets as bare files (never read by an agent; AGENTS.md absolute 4).
.env/

# ⚠ A research corpus is NOT ignored. A corpus in an ignored directory is lost
# with the machine, and a conclusion nobody can re-check is an opinion
# (docs/methodology/research.md section 3.4). Where one is too large for every
# clone, it goes in GHCR as an artifact and the write-up names its digest.
